# unscii-icons: Unscii-8 at 8x8 cells for the small panels of the minspec
# build, with a chosen list of Nerd Fonts' icons and color emoji. Unscii-8
# draws the text, from a BDF file, and its shapes follow the IBM PC's code
# page 437 font. The two small layers add the icons that shell prompts and
# file listers draw and the emoji that terminals show most.
#
# Unscii-8 is published as a .hex file, which the font helper does not
# read, so the source names a BDF file converted from it. When that file is
# missing, vtium's built-in font draws the text in the same 8x8 cell. GNU
# Unifont, the last layer, holds 8x16 glyphs, which do not fit an 8x8 cell,
# so the built-in font draws every character that the sources before it
# lack. vtium ships this font set, never the fonts.
#
# Licenses: Unscii-8 is in the public domain. The layers name their own
# licenses.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D3: the small panels category.
# - ADR-1204 D8: the BDF file converted from Unscii-8's .hex file.

name=unscii-icons
cell=8x8
license=OFL-1.1 AND MIT

# The text, Unscii-8 2.1 converted to BDF.
source=bdf:/usr/share/fonts/vtium/unscii-8.bdf
version=2.1
url=http://viznut.fi/unscii/

layer=nerd-symbols-small
layer=noto-emoji-small
layer=unifont
